<%# A block inside a review card that is NOT part of what the card is deciding — a
    report on the read, a note, anything that does not post with the card's form.

    It sets itself apart by KIND rather than by weight, because the card body is
    borderless by design: every input draws its own underline, so a rule between them
    is indistinguishable from one more field. Hence a recessed ground and a heading.
    `action` is the button that acts on what is in here, kept with its own controls
    rather than in the card's action bar, which holds only the terminal decisions. %>
<%# locals: (title:, action: nil) %>
<aside class="card-aside">
  <h2 class="card-aside__title"><%= title %></h2>
  <%= yield %>
  <%= tag.div(action, class: "card-aside__actions") if action.present? %>
</aside>
